Next, update the CSS for the layout of .entry.has-img, .thumb, .entry-body, .thesis.has-img. Let's add the following rules to style.css:

- `.entry` is currently `padding: 14px 2px; border-bottom: dashed`. In the case of has-img, make it display: flex; gap; align-items flex-start.
- `.entry-body { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }`
- `.thumb { flex: 0 0 auto; width: 120px; }` img { width:120px; height:160px; object-fit:cover; border-radius:10px; border:1px solid line; display:block; }
- `.thumb:hover img { transform: scale(1.03); }` (subtle effect) with transition applied.
- `.thesis.has-img { display:flex; gap:18px; align-items:flex-start; }`
- Responsive: for small screens, should the thumb be smaller (e.g., 90px), or the image be moved? Keep it on the left side but make it smaller. Actually, at narrow widths keep the image and shrink it to width 84px / height 112px.

Let's add these rules to style.css. Append them near the publications/thesis sections. Let's add them at the end of the file (before responsive), or in the appropriate place. To make it manageable, I'll add a new block at the end and adjust within @media.

Let's append the CSS rules.

What to add:

```
/* ----------------------------- thumbnails (publications and thesis) */
.entry.has-img,
.thesis.has-img {
  display: flex;
  gap: 18px;
  align-items: flex-start;
}
.thumb {
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  display: block;
  width: 120px;
  line-height: 0;
}
.thumb img {
  width: 120px;
  height: 160px;
  object-fit: cover;
  object-position: top center;
  border-radius: 10px;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  transition: transform .18s ease, box-shadow .18s ease;
}
.thumb:hover img {
  transform: translateY(-2px) scale(1.02);
  box-shadow: 0 10px 26px rgba(28,27,24,.14);
}
.entry-body { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
.thesis .t, .thesis .d, .thesis .actions { max-width: 100%; }
```

And in the responsive section:
```
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .thumb, .thumb img { width: 92px; }
  .thumb img { height: 122px; }
  .entry.has-img, .thesis.has-img { gap: 12px; }
}
```

